<div class="container page-body">
	<div class="page-layout"><article class="page-content">
		<p class="page-lead">NIJOSTAM welcomes original work that is not under consideration elsewhere. Manuscripts are evaluated for technical correctness, relevance, clarity, significance and presentation.</p>
		<h2 class="section-title"><ion-icon name="clipboard-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon> Before you submit</h2><ul class="icon-list"><li><ion-icon name="checkmark-circle-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon>Prepare an anonymous manuscript without author-identifying information.</li><li><ion-icon name="checkmark-circle-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon>Upload a separate title page with author names, affiliations, email addresses and corresponding-author details.</li><li><ion-icon name="checkmark-circle-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon>Include an abstract of no more than 250 words and four to five keywords.</li><li><ion-icon name="checkmark-circle-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon>Use clear English, single-column layout and APA 7th edition references.</li><li><ion-icon name="checkmark-circle-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon>Disclose funding, competing interests and applicable ethics approvals.</li></ul>
		<h2 class="section-title"><ion-icon name="documents-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon> Article types</h2><div class="guideline-grid"><section><h3>Original research</h3><p>Empirical research, including null results, replications and refutations. Recommended length: 3,000–6,000 words.</p></section><section><h3>Short research articles</h3><p>Focused research notes with concise methods and results, supported by relevant figures or tables.</p></section><section><h3>Reviews</h3><p>Critical syntheses of published research. Full reviews are generally 5,000–9,000 words.</p></section><section><h3>Short communications</h3><p>Concise reports of timely findings, typically 2,500–3,500 words.</p></section><section><h3>Minireviews</h3><p>Accessible overviews of an emerging topic or a defined area of recent progress.</p></section><section><h3>Letters to the editor</h3><p>Brief scholarly responses or clarifications, limited to 600 words excluding references.</p></section></div>
		<h2 class="section-title"><ion-icon name="shield-checkmark-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon> Review and publication</h2><p>Online submission is handled through the journal’s author portal. Accepted manuscripts proceed to publication after peer review and editorial checks.</p>
		<h2 class="section-title"><ion-icon name="pricetag-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon> Publication charge</h2><p>The listed article processing charge is ₦25,000 for Nigerian authors and $30 for international authors. Confirm current fees with the editorial office before submitting.</p>
		<div class="notice-band"><strong><ion-icon name="rocket-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon> Ready to submit?</strong><span>Account registration and manuscript submission are handled by the official journal platform.</span><a href="https://nijostam.org/journals/index.php/njstm/about/submissions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open submission portal <ion-icon name="open-outline" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon></a></div>
